<title>INDIA: India sugar prices rise on fresh consumer buying.</title>
<headline>India sugar prices rise on fresh consumer buying.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian sugar prices rose on Monday on renewed consumer buying and restricted arrivals, dealers said.</p>
<p>S-30 sugar rose by five rupees to 1,250/1,285 rupees per quintal while M-30 rose by 15 rupees to 1,290/1,330 rupees.</p>
<p>&quot;Sugar arrivals from mills remained low due to scattered availability of trucks at producing centres,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
